timeline.body:
> ref. stomp-websocket.js fragmented frames sending [impl](https://github.com/jmesnil/stomp-websocket/blob/3b60a70bdb94ae34e7a2891e5ca8c50ed6e2b751/lib/stomp.js#L162-L165)

```js
//  stomp-websocket.js
      while (true) {
        if (out.length > this.maxWebSocketFrameSize) {
          this.ws.send(out.substring(0, this.maxWebSocketFrameSize));
          out = out.substring(this.maxWebSocketFrameSize);
```
FYI) same with other STOMP library, all we need here is simply split message that exceed `bufferSizeLimit`!

Thanks to our `BuffringStompDecoder.java`, we can reassemble these incomplete frames well.

(I checked receiving reassembled message well by adding `reassembleReceivedIFragmentedFrames` test on `WebSocketStompClientTest` 🙇)

